    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Outcome: resolve_funding. The manuscript is not ready for submission to PLOS because no funding statement has been entered. PLOS requires one, so this is a definite blocker that must be fixed first.\n\nThe other checks are satisfied on the supplied evidence:\n- **Exclusivity:** the work has appeared only as a preprint and is not under consideration at another journal.\n- **Author approval:** every listed author has approved the submitted version.\n- **Data:** the data and metadata are in a named repository, and the data statement gives the persistent identifier.\n- **Competing interests:** all relevant potential competing interests are disclosed.\n- **Code:** no analysis relied on code the authors wrote themselves.\n\nOne item should be followed up separately. The community group that recruited participants has asked for an extra community data-sharing review before publication, and the evidence does not say whether it is complete. This is a request to the data office, not a PLOS data-availability requirement, and the PLOS data requirement already appears met. It should be confirmed with Anika Rossi or the data office before submission, but it does not change the recorded outcome.\n\nThe press office schedule request does not resolve any readiness check, so it should not set the submission timing. Next step: Sanjay Singh should enter the funding statement, with Fatima Meyer confirming the grant details.",
